    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule following the repository's existing convention for create-time, count-derived owner fields (exactly like `namesakeCount` and `customerCode`).\n\n**Behavior:** When an owner is created, if more than 80 owners already carry the same adjusted business-day `registrationDate`, the new owner is created with `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`. This reuses the same per-day accumulation path as the existing daily-limit rule (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`), so the warning window is 81\u2013100 owners for a given day.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` at build time).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter and a `bulk_signup_warning` `@Column`.\n3. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table.\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added the `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and an `assignBulkSignupWarning(owner)` step in `addOwner`, computed before persistence so it counts only pre-existing owners for the day. MapStruct auto-maps the field to the DTO by name, so it's present (never null) on both the create and GET responses.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` (fresh-create \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` = false) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
